Third-party components
----------------------
Kerotakis links or embeds the following in its released web and native apps.
Summaries here do not replace the licence texts. The app includes the complete
dependency inventory and every available licence/notice file from those
packages under About -> Open-source licences. That bundled document is the
package-level record; this NOTICE highlights the principal components.

Currently shipped
- IPhreeqc / PHREEQC — USGS User Rights Notice (public-domain-like, U.S.
  Geological Survey). IPhreeqc is by S.R. Charlton and D.L. Parkhurst;
  PHREEQC is by D.L. Parkhurst and C.A.J. Appelo. Aqueous speciation, mineral
  saturation, gas partitioning and redox are built from the pinned vendored
  source and its thermodynamic databases (phreeqc.dat, wateq4f.dat,
  minteq.v4.dat and pitzer.dat). Kerotakis modifies the build integration and
  BASIC runtime; it is not an unmodified USGS distribution.
- MY-BASIC — MIT, Copyright (c) 2011–2026 Tony Wang. Pinned language core
  for PHREEQC BASIC programs (rate expressions, user punch/print, calculated
  values). Default in all Kerotakis builds.
- NASA CEA thermodynamic data and code — Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) 2025,
  United States Government as represented by the Administrator of the
  National Aeronautics and Space Administration. The embedded `thermo.inp`
  supplies NASA-9 gas and condensed-phase thermochemistry.
- diffsol — MIT, Copyright (c) Martin Robinson. Stiff ODE/DAE integration for
  reaction kinetics.
- chematic — MIT OR Apache-2.0, authored by kent-tokyo. Structure parsing,
  reaction templates and the wasm-compatible molecular identity path.
- Svelte — MIT, Copyright (c) 2016–2025 Svelte Contributors. User interface.
- Rust crates and native-shell dependencies — licences include MIT,
  Apache-2.0, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, ISC, Zlib, Unicode, Unlicense and
  other expressions named in the bundled inventory. The in-app open-source
  licence document names every package, version, declared licence, authors and
  repository and reproduces each licence/notice file present in its package.

Curated data
- Kerotakis-authored chemistry data shipped in official binaries (the codex:
  reactions, observations, register copy, colour and property curation) is
  licensed CC BY 4.0, separately from the AGPL-3.0 code. Imported CC0 records,
  including the oehTopics curriculum vocabulary, remain CC0 1.0 and name
  their source per record. No CC BY-SA data is bundled in official apps.
- Where curated data incorporates or is checked against third-party datasets,
  those are named with their own terms per record — and where an upstream's
  licence claim appears inconsistent with its own sources, Kerotakis honours
  the original source's terms.

Reactivity screening
- The reactive-group compatibility screen is Kerotakis' own implementation of
  the methodology published in open-access literature by NOAA's Office of
  Response and Restoration with the EPA and the Center for Chemical Process
  Safety. It does not contain or reproduce the CAMEO Chemicals database or any
  of its contributed proprietary fields.

Reviewed ligand equilibrium constants
- U.S. Bureau of Mines IC 9429 (1995), Charles M. Flynn, Jr. and Sandra M.
  Haslem, Cyanide Chemistry — Precious Metals Processing and Waste Treatment.
  Six 25 °C, zero-ionic-strength complex formation constants transcribed from
  Tables D-7 and D-15. CDC Stacks explicitly identifies the report as Public
  Domain: https://stacks.cdc.gov/view/cdc/206360 . See the per-field review in
  provenance/usbm-ic9429-complexes-review.md. No spectra or rates are supplied.

Reviewed hydrogen bromide gas uptake
- Rolf Sander (2023), Compilation of Henry's law constants (version 5.0.0)
  for water as solvent, Atmospheric Chemistry and Physics 23, 10901-12440,
  https://doi.org/10.5194/acp-23-10901-2023 . Copyright Author(s) 2023,
  licensed Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International:
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ . Only HBr note 146's
  reference constant and temperature slope are used. Changes: converted
  concentration/pressure units and derived a local reaction enthalpy using
  the USGS PHREEQC pure-water density formulation. No endorsement implied.
  See provenance/sander-2023-hbr-review.md for conditions and omissions.

Reviewed stainless-steel hydrogen-evolution kinetics
- M. C. van Ede and U. Angst (2024), Tafel slopes and exchange current
  densities of oxygen reduction and hydrogen evolution on steel,
  https://doi.org/10.1177/1478422X241227829 . Copyright the authors,
  licensed Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International:
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ . Three same-condition
  cathodic HER rows from Supplementary Table B1 and three same-condition ORR
  rows from Supplementary Table C1 are used. Changes: arithmetic means and
  observed min/max were computed in SI units. No endorsement
  implied. See provenance/van-ede-2024-her-review.md.

Reviewed Q345R corrosion-model candidates
- Han et al. (2018), Corrosion Behaviors of Q345R Steel at the Initial Stage
  in an Oxygen-Containing Aqueous Environment: Experiment and Modeling,
  https://doi.org/10.3390/ma11081462 . Copyright the authors, licensed Creative
  Commons Attribution 4.0 International:
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ . Published equations and
  parameter values are represented as quarantined, non-runtime candidates;
  their condition scaling and validity geometry were generalized. No
  endorsement implied. See
  provenance/electrochemical-model-extension-review.md.

Reviewed additional-solvent distillation reference fields
- U.S. Coast Guard CHRIS manual (June 1999), methanol (MAL) and isopropanol
  (IPA), sections 9.2, 9.3 and 9.12: molar mass, normal boiling point and
  latent heat. U.S. government physical-property information; see
  https://www.uscg.mil/disclaim/ and the original NOAA-hosted manual PDFs
  https://cameochemicals.noaa.gov/chris/MAL.pdf and
  https://cameochemicals.noaa.gov/chris/IPA.pdf . This narrow slice excludes
  third-party restricted categories and is not a CAMEO database export.
  Unit conversion and a bounded constant-latent ideal-mixture approximation
  are Kerotakis modifications, not government predictions or endorsement.
  See provenance/uscg-chris-still-review.md for the limits.

